<h2>What Matters by Trade</h2>
<h3>Roofing</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> Before/after galleries and insurance claim messaging</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> Homeowners frequently collect multiple bids before choosing, so trust signals and portfolio quality carry outsized weight</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> "We Work With All Insurance Companies" messaging resonates strongly, since most roofing jobs are insurance claims</li>
<li><strong>Mobile behavior:</strong> Mobile-dominant, but with a meaningfully higher share of desktop research traffic than emergency trades</li>
</ul>
<h3>HVAC</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> Emergency service pages and maintenance plan CTAs</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> Split between emergency repairs (high urgency) and system replacement (longer research cycle) — the two need very different page treatments</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> Visible financing options noticeably lift contact rates on replacement pages</li>
<li><strong>Seasonal variation:</strong> Emergency page performance swings heavily with the season — expect surges in peak heating and cooling months</li>
</ul>
<h3>Plumbing</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> 24/7 emergency messaging and sticky call buttons</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> The highest emergency-intent trade — most visitors are already in crisis mode and will call the first credible option they find</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> A specific response-time promise ("30-Minute Arrival") builds urgency and trust simultaneously</li>
<li><strong>Mobile behavior:</strong> The most mobile-heavy trade of the group, by a wide margin</li>
</ul>
<h3>Electrical</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> License display and safety messaging</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> Safety concerns and licensing credibility weigh heavily, since electrical work carries real risk</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> Specific credentials ("Licensed Master Electrician") outperform generic "Licensed &amp; Insured" language</li>
<li><strong>Mobile behavior:</strong> Mobile-heavy with a strong emergency segment</li>
</ul>
<h3>Solar</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> Financing information and state incentive content</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> The longest sales cycle and highest research intent of any trade covered here — visitors are comparing multiple companies over weeks, not hours</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> Interactive solar calculator tools noticeably increase time-on-page and quote requests</li>
<li><strong>Mobile behavior:</strong> More desktop research traffic than any other trade in this list</li>
</ul>
<h3>Restoration</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Highest-impact element:</strong> Emergency response time and insurance direct-billing messaging</li>
<li><strong>Buying behavior:</strong> Crisis-driven and insurance-backed — speed and insurance handling matter more than price comparison</li>
<li><strong>What works:</strong> "We Bill Your Insurance Directly" messaging removes a major point of friction</li>
<li><strong>Mobile behavior:</strong> Mobile-dominant; crisis-driven searches dominate</li>
</ul>
