<h2>Common Mistakes We See (and How to Fix Them)</h2>
<h3>Mistake 1: The Brochure Website</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Digital-brochure sites — pretty design, no conversion infrastructure. No sticky CTA, no trust signals above the fold, no click-to-call.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Add one sticky element and one trust signal this week. Start with the tap-to-call button.</p>
<h3>Mistake 2: Stock Photo Syndrome</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Obvious stock photography — generic smiling families, pristine houses, model-perfect workers.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Replace the hero image with a real team photo. Use a smartphone if needed. Authenticity beats perfection.</p>
<h3>Mistake 3: The Contact Us CTA</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Generic "Contact Us" or "Learn More" buttons where a benefit-driven CTA should be.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Use action-oriented, benefit-driven CTAs: "Get My Free Estimate," "Call Now for Same-Day Service," "Book Online in 60 Seconds."</p>
<h3>Mistake 4: Hidden Phone Numbers</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Phone numbers buried in the footer or tucked away on a contact page only.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Phone number in the header (desktop), header + sticky button (mobile), on every page.</p>
<h3>Mistake 5: Form Overload</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Contact forms padded with extra fields — budget range, preferred time, project description — before the visitor has committed to anything.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Trim to 4 fields: Name, Phone, Email, Service Needed. Ask for details after they submit.</p>
<h3>Mistake 6: No Emergency Pages</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> HVAC, plumbing, and electrical sites with no dedicated emergency service page at all.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Create one emergency page per trade with urgent CTA, response time promise, and after-hours routing.</p>
<h3>Mistake 7: Slow Hosting</h3>
<p><strong>What we see:</strong> Slow-loading mobile pages, usually the result of cheap shared hosting and unoptimized images.</p>
<p><strong>The fix:</strong> Move to quality hosting (WP Engine, Kinsta, SiteGround), compress all images, implement caching.</p>
